[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:A Spot of Bother]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.48]Lesson 58 | 第58课
[00:02.48]A spot of bother | 一点小麻烦
[00:09.52]What did the old lady find when she got home? | 老太太回到家时发现了什么？
[00:14.73]The old lady was glad to be back at the block of flats where she lived. | 老太太回到她居住的公寓楼时，心里很高兴。
[00:20.86]Her shopping had tired her and her basket had grown heavier with every step of the way home. | 购物让她疲惫不堪，回家的路上，篮子仿佛每走一步就沉一分。
[00:28.27]In the lift her thoughts were on lunch and a good rest; | 在电梯里，她一心想着午饭和好好休息；
[00:32.65]but when she got out at her own floor, both were forgotten in her sudden discovery that her front door was open. | 可到了自己那层楼走出电梯时，却突然发现前门开着，午饭和休息顿时都忘到了脑后。
[00:42.07]She was thinking that she must reprimand her home help the next morning for such a monstrous piece of negligence, | 她正想着第二天早上一定要训斥一顿家务女佣如此严重的失职，
[00:50.44]when she remembered that she had gone shopping after the home help had left and she knew that she had turned both keys in their locks. | 忽然想起买完东西回来时家务女佣早已走了，而且她清楚地记得自己用钥匙在两把锁上锁了门。
[01:00.63]She walked slowly into the hall and at once noticed that all the room doors were open, | 她慢慢走进门厅，立刻发现所有的房门都开着，
[01:07.58]yet following her regular practice she had shut them before going out. | 而按照她的习惯，出门前她是把门都关好的。
[01:12.69]Looking into the drawing room, she saw a scene of confusion over by her writing desk. | 向客厅里看去，她看到写字台旁边一片凌乱。
[01:19.28]It was as clear as daylight then that burglars had forced an entry during her absence. | 事情再清楚不过了：她不在家时，窃贼曾闯进门来。
[01:25.89]Her first impulse was to go round all the rooms looking for the thieves, | 她的第一个冲动是到各个房间去找窃贼，
[01:31.23]but then she decided that at her age it might be more prudent to have someone with her, | 但她随即想到，以她这样的年纪，找个人陪着更稳妥，
[01:37.62]so she went to fetch the porter from his basement. | 于是她到地下室去找门房。
[01:41.71]By this time her legs were beginning to tremble, so she sat down and accepted a cup of very strong tea, while he telephoned the police. | 这时她的双腿开始发抖，于是她坐了下来，接受了一杯浓茶，由门房去打电话报警。
[01:52.27]Then, her composure regained, she was ready to set off with the porter's assistance to search for any intruders who might still be lurking in her flat. | 然后，她恢复了镇静，准备在门房的陪同下，搜查一下可能仍潜伏在她公寓里的不速之客。
[02:04.54]They went through the rooms, being careful to touch nothing, | 他们查遍了一个个房间，小心翼翼不去碰任何东西，
[02:08.73]as they did not want to hinder the police in their search for fingerprints. | 因为不想妨碍警察寻找指纹。
[02:13.88]The chaos was inconceivable. | 混乱的状况难以想象。
[02:17.27]She had lived in the flat for thirty years and was a veritable magpie at hoarding: | 她在这套公寓里住了30年，又是个名副其实的收藏破烂的“喜鹊”：
[02:23.59]and it seemed as though everything she possessed had been tossed out and turned over and over. | 仿佛她拥有的每样东西都被翻出来，倒了个底朝天。
[02:31.08]At least sorting out the things she should have discarded years ago was now being made easier for her. | 至少，她早就该扔掉的那些东西，如今扔起来倒是容易多了。
[02:38.73]Then a police inspector arrived with a constable and she told them of her discovery of the ransacked flat. | 接着，一名警探带着一名警察来了，她把公寓被洗劫一空的事告诉了他们。
[02:47.15]The inspector began to look for fingerprints, while the constable checked that the front door locks had not been forced, | 警探开始寻找指纹，警察则检查前门锁是否被撬过，
[02:54.40]thereby proving that the burglars had either used skeleton keys or entered over the balcony. | 从而证明窃贼要么用了万能钥匙，要么就是从阳台进来的。
[03:02.03]There was no trace of fingerprints, but the inspector found a dirty red bundle that contained jewellery which the old lady said was not hers. | 没有指纹的痕迹，但警探发现了一个脏兮兮的红色包裹，里面装有珠宝，老太太说不是她的。
[03:13.07]So their entry into this flat was apparently not the burglars' first job that day and they must have been disturbed. | 所以窃贼闯进这套公寓显然不是当天头一回作案，他们准是被打断了。
[03:21.84]The inspector then asked the old lady to try to check what was missing by the next day, | 警探接着请老太太在第二天之前设法清点丢失的东西，
[03:28.20]and advised her not to stay alone in the flat for a few nights. | 并建议她几夜之内不要独自待在公寓里。
[03:32.11]The old lady thought he was a fussy creature, | 老太太觉得他是个大惊小怪的家伙，
[03:36.47]but since the porter agreed with him, she rang up her daughter and asked for her help in what she described as a little spot of bother. | 但由于门房也同意他的意见，她便给女儿打了电话，请她来帮忙处理她所描述的“一点小麻烦”。
